The task is to push a new build of an edge function (a Worker) and make it live. The first listed tool that fits is workers_legacy_scripts_update, which uploads a worker module. The wrangler skill is also possible, but it only applies to projects that have a Wrangler config, and I don't know whether this one does. A direct tool call is the more reliable start. The wrangler skill would be better if the project uses Wrangler.

Which tool to use depends on the Worker setup. The versions workflow needs workers_versions_create followed by workers_deployments_create. workers_legacy_scripts_update uploads and deploys in one step, so it makes the build live right away.

